-- Today's data, as the Increment 1 code writes it (a database at inc1a: 0_baseline + inc1a applied),
-- for the first Increment 2 release (inc1b_contract + inc2_driver_flow). Loaded with `prisma db execute`
-- after `prisma migrate deploy` of the inc1a release.
--
--   AG (Ahmed Gas): a store, Rs 5,000 after a top-up of Rs 6,000, a delivered order (Rs 400), a cancelled
--     one (Rs 600 deducted, then returned) and an assigned one on a PLANNED run; customers Sana and Usman.
--   BG (Bilal Gas): a store, Rs 0, one pending order; customer Hina; an old refused manual top-up still
--     FAILED (inc1b relabels it REJECTED).
--   Runs: T1 COMPLETED (DR1, LEA-101), T2 PLANNED (DR2, LEB-202), T3 ABORTED. None in progress.
--   AG's cylinders, created in this order (their short numbers will be 1 to 5):
--     A1 FULL in the store, no events (registered in Inc 1, which wrote none)           → last_event_id NULL
--     A2 FULL with Sana: loaded and delivered on T1                                         → its DELIVERED
--     A3 EMPTY in the store: loaded, delivered, taken back and handed back on T1            → its SCAN_IN
--     A4 FULL on LEA-101: loaded on T1 and left on the van                                  → its SCAN_OUT
--     A5 FULL in the store, but its newest event says it went to Sana (the holder was fixed by hand)
--                                                                                           → NULL
--   A6 and A7 share one created_at: the id decides their numbers (6, then 7).
--   BG's cylinder B1 FULL in its store, no events                                         → short_no 1.

